      "tag": "external_military_pressure",
      "layer": "military_security",
      "description": "Edward I's systematic castle-building program, the 'Iron Ring' of castles (Caernarfon, Harlech, Conwy, Beaumaris), pacified Wales by controlling the coastal supply routes and choking off the mountain interior; no medieval Welsh force could besiege these castles",
